MODIFICATIONS
-------------

The upstream client was rebranded and reconfigured. No functional change was
made to the tunnel, the protocol, or the cryptography.

1.  Names and identifiers. The application name, bundle identifiers, app group,
    mach service name, URL scheme, on-disk support directory, configuration
    filename, keychain service and os_log subsystems were changed from the
    upstream vendor's to ZTARC's. These are not cosmetic: sharing an app group
    or a bundle identifier with an installed upstream client would put two
    products in one container.

2.  Artwork. The application icon, menu bar icons, logo and accent colour were
    replaced. Two onboarding screenshots showing the upstream product were
    removed along with the views that displayed them.

3.  iOS. The two iOS targets were removed from the Xcode project. ZTARC ships a
    macOS client.

4.  Default server. The login window defaults to https://console.ztarc.io
    instead of the upstream vendor's hosted service, which ZTARC has no access
    to and does not operate.

5.  Legal links. Links to the upstream vendor's Terms of Service and Privacy
    Policy were removed, together with two lines asking the user to agree to
    them. Those documents describe the upstream vendor's service and their
    handling of user data; neither statement is ZTARC's to make. A link to this
    program's source was added in their place, in the tray menu and the About
    tab.

6.  Automatic updates. The Sparkle updater is not started, and the update feed
    URL and update-signing public key were removed from the application's
    Info.plist. The feed was a host ZTARC does not control and the key was not
    ZTARC's; leaving either in place would have meant a third party could ship
    updates into every installation.

7.  Build configuration. The upstream vendor's Apple Developer team identifier
    and provisioning profile names were removed, and the Sparkle dependency was
    pinned to an exact version rather than a range.


THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

The following are used by this program and are not covered by its licence.
They are not modified, and are redistributed under their own terms.

  Sparkle                 MIT                 https://sparkle-project.org
  github.com/fosrl/olm    AGPL-3              the tunnel engine
  github.com/fosrl/newt   AGPL-3              connection handling
  WireGuard-go            MIT                 via olm
  gVisor                  Apache-2.0          via olm

The Go runtime is patched during the build with
PangolinGo/goruntime-boottime-over-monotonic.diff, carried in the upstream
repository, which makes Go's monotonic clock survive system sleep. The patch is
applied to a private copy of GOROOT and does not modify the installed Go
toolchain.
